  question          `mask-unaffordable` says blocking a quarter of the F1
                    group costs 59% of the lesson, for TWO reasons it could
                    not separate: blocked neurons still PERTURB, and they are
                    still READ. Which one is it?
  why it matters    a separate readout -- the mushroom body's motif, one
                    population read and taught independently per compartment
                    -- removes both. That build changes the larynx decoder,
                    which is a transducer, so it wants a number first.
  the decomposition `set_explore_block` silences exploration on a range
                    without touching anything else. Freeze alone is (a)+(b);
                    freeze AND silence is (b). The difference is (a), exactly.
  the refusal       if `w75` costs nothing against `w100`, this genome is not
                    reproducing the condition and there is no cost to split.
                    36 seeds.

